view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "jobs_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/werf/werf/actions/runs/36858580652/jobs", "logs_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/werf/werf/actions/runs/36858580652/logs", "check_suite_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/werf/werf/check-suites/99830405213", "artifacts_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/werf/werf/actions/runs/36858580652/artifacts", "cancel_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/werf/werf/actions/runs/36858580652/cancel", "rerun_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/werf/werf/actions/runs/36858580652/rerun", "previous_attempt_url": null, "workflow_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/werf/werf/actions/workflows/21332", "head_commit": {"id": "29abab142f80b811e9fd569017062cfb1f887288", "tree_id": "68a1dba3a50179a78d82f0bc2d3687e7ac56d51a", "message": "fix(build): report invalid .dockerignore patterns without panicking (#7992)\n\n## Summary\n\nA committed ignore pattern ending in a backslash previously made `werf\nbuild` panic with `syntax error in pattern`. Builds now return an error\nidentifying the selected ignore file and invalid pattern.\n\nReproduce with a reachable Docker backend:\n\n```sh\nmkdir dockerignore-repro && cd dockerignore-repro\ngit init -q\nprintf 'project: ignore-error\\nconfigVersion: 1\\n---\\nimage: app\\ndockerfile: Dockerfile\\nstaged: false\\n' > werf.yaml\nprintf 'FROM scratch\\n' > Dockerfile\nprintf '%s\\n' Dockerfile 'archive-old\\' > .dockerignore\ngit add .\ngit -c user.name=Test -c user.email=test@example.com -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -qm repro\nwerf build --repo=:local\n```\n\n## What\n\n- Invalid patterns in `.dockerignore`, `Dockerfile.dockerignore`,\n`.containerignore`, and `Dockerfile.containerignore` produce a normal\nbuild error naming the file and pattern.\n- Patterns rejected during lazy compilation, including exclusions such\nas `![z-a]`, fail during matcher creation instead of panicking during\npath matching.\n- VERIFIED: the reproducer exits with code 1 and reports `read ignore\nfile \".dockerignore\": parse ignore pattern \"archive-old\\\\\": syntax error\nin pattern` without a panic.\n- Valid matching, ignore-file selection order, Dockerfile reinclusion,\nand cache identities remain unchanged; `.gitignore` continues to be\ninterpreted by Git.\n\n## Why\n\nThe matcher constructor panicked on user-supplied syntax errors, and\nMoby defers some pattern compilation until matching. Validate every\npattern before exposing the matcher and propagate errors through the\nexisting build error path so users can locate and correct the rule.\n\nSigned-off-by: Aleksei Igrychev <aleksei.igrychev@palark.com>", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T11:56:58Z", "author": {"name": "Aleksei Igrychev", "email": "aleksei.igrychev@palark.com"}, "committer": {"name": "GitHub", "email": "noreply@github.com"}}, "repository": {"id": 50365232, "node_id": "MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk1MDM2NTIzMg==", "name": "werf", "full_name": "werf/werf", "private": false, "owner": {"login": "werf", "id": 66415983, "node_id": "MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjY2NDE1OTgz", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66415983?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/werf", "html_url": "https://github.com/werf", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/werf/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/werf/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/werf/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/werf/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/werf/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/werf/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/werf/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/werf/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/werf/received_events", "type": "Organization", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "html_url": "https://github.com/werf/werf", "description": "A solution for implementing 